# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# A credential pushed once is compromised even if the next commit removes it —
# it stays in the history, in every clone, and in GitHub's fork network. The
# env rules below are therefore deny-first: everything matching .env is
# excluded, and .env.example is re-admitted by name because it is deliberately
# all empty keys.
#
# `node scripts/secret-scan.mjs` checks the actual bytes rather than trusting
# that this file was written correctly. Run it before any commit that touches
# configuration.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*secret*
*credential*
!scripts/secret-scan.mjs

# ── Dependencies and build products ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── QA and audit OUTPUT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The instruments are committed — scripts/*.mjs is how every claim in the
# README was measured, and a claim whose measurement cannot be re-run is an
# assertion. It is only what they print that is excluded: those numbers are
# specific to one machine at one moment, and a stale committed report is worse
# than no report.
lighthouse/
reports/
*.lhr.json
lh-*.json
lighthouse-*.json
.lighthouseci/
a11y-*.json
reveal-*.json
meta-*.json
i18n-*.json
*-report.json
*-report.md
!MEDIA-MANIFEST.md

# ── Photo-search harvests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Output of scripts/car-pool.mjs and scripts/car-finalists.mjs: preview frames
# pulled from Pexels, Unsplash and Pixabay while choosing the car placeholder.
# Third-party photographs that were looked at and rejected have no business in
# this repository. The one frame actually chosen is committed, in public/media.
candidates/
car-pool/
car-candidates/
fiat-finalists.png
contact-sheet*.png
contact-sheet*.jpg

# ── Screenshots and scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/shots/
/screens/
*.local

# ── Editor and OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── Unreferenced photography ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The library was mirrored wholesale from the property's own sites, so public/
# holds more than the site renders. The referenced set — including the mirrored
# suite photographs — is committed; these are duplicates at other crops and
# frames that lost their edit. Regenerate this list with
# `node scripts/media-manifest.mjs`, which resolves references from src/,
# sanity/ and scripts/, including the generated maps components index into.
# See MEDIA-MANIFEST.md.
/public/media/1d15d8544b80b9780aa76665a6ebab60.webp
/public/media/539843e1947b4911ffbb344d074ad3d1.webp
/public/media/6838240023f27d1dfbe9bf539e458d02.webp
/public/media/7d159bbd00f3a06c3982ad3dfaa76cca.webp
/public/media/94dce1948a5167baeb0bc848894477cf.webp
/public/media/a7c7c8cb46171d21151836d335e55b3a.webp
/public/media/c4be1a238eab273f5cebc725d306a4cb.webp
/public/media/d16518235dd4d28125a771445ca67988.webp
/public/media/e7684dae57efc05b520aa96da1fd547c.webp

.vercel
.env*
